==Icelandic==
===Etymology===
From the term ''skjör-ost'' in {{term|w:en:Funen|Fjón|Funen}} in {{term|w:en:Denmark|Denmark}}. The Latin term {{term||lac concretum}} in [[w:Germania (book)|the book Germania]] by [[w:Tacitus|Tacitus]].
===Noun===
'''skyr''' {{n}} ([[skyrs]])
# [[#English|skyr]]; a [[yogurt]]-like product made of [[curdled]] [[milk]], [[curd]]s stored up for food; a thick dairy product unique to Icelandic cuisine that can be traced back to the [[Viking]]s

====Derived terms====
*[[berjaskyr]] (blackberries and curds)
*[[skyraskur]] (a curd bowl)
*[[skyrbúr]] (a curd bower)
*[[skyrker]] (a curd vessel)

